*   **Space**: $O(N)$ for vertex storage.
*   **Numerical Stability**: Hybrid architecture ensures $\mathcal{O}(\epsilon_{machine})$ relative error for all scales. L'Huilier's theorem on the Authalic sphere provides exact ellipsoidal area equivalence (Gauss-Bonnet) for large polygons. Local ENU projection (Shoelace) eliminates catastrophic cancellation for micro-polygons ($< 1 \text{ km}$ perimeter), guaranteeing $\text{mm}^2$ precision for drone photogrammetry grids.

